<Layout title="About - Bin Stores USA" description="About Bin Stores USA: a links directory of bin stores in the United States. No advice, no ratings, no checks. Listings come from public sources.">
  <h1>About Bin Stores USA</h1>
  <p>Bin Stores USA is a links directory for bin stores in the United States. A bin store is a shop that sells returned goods and overstock from big retailers, with the goods placed in large bins.</p>
  <h2>What this site does</h2>
  <p>Each listing has a store name, a city and state, a street address when a public source lists one, and a link to a public listing for that store. That is all. The site does not sell anything, take bookings, or collect store data from visitors.</p>
  <h2>What this site does not do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>It gives no shopping advice.</li>
    <li>It does not rate, rank, check, or vouch for any store.</li>
    <li>It does not list prices, hours, or restock days, because they change often.</li>
    <li>It does not list a store it could not find in a public source.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Where listings come from</h2>
  <p>Listings come from public sources such as TheBinMap, BinStoresFinder, BinStoreFinder, FindTheBin, GoodwillBins.org, local guides, and store sites. Each listing on this site names its source and the date it was checked. If a store closes or moves, the listing may be out of date, so check the store's own page before you go.</p>
  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>If a listing is wrong or a store has closed, the store's own page is the best place to check. This site is a simple directory of links, and listings are updated when public sources change.</p>
</Layout>
